<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-222 Phase 2 prerequisite (nexus-yye8l.21): nexus.request_ledger_tenants, the set of tenants that have
    ever held a request_ledger row, so the retention arm can visit every one of them.

    THE PROBLEM. The retention arm deletes a tenant's old ledger rows one tenant at a time (RequestLedger.retain,
    under withTenant), so it needs a tenant list. nexus.request_ledger is FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY, so under
    nexus_svc (NOSUPERUSER NOBYPASSRLS) a SELECT DISTINCT tenant_id with no tenant stamp returns nothing; the
    list cannot come from the ledger itself. It came from the reaper's tenants (the default tenant plus every
    tenant in service_tokens), so a tenant that lost its last token (a scope=data JIT token row is deleted 7 days
    after it expires) kept its ledger rows for ever. A test that read the ledger as the superuser would have
    "worked" and proved nothing (the vectors-029 header says the same about a superuser-run migration).

    THE TABLE. One row per tenant, written by the claim path in the same transaction as the tenant's ledger
    insert (INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING), so a ledger row cannot exist without its tenant row. The
    primary key is the index the enumeration uses (a full scan of a table with one row per tenant, bounded by
    the statement timeout the retention arm already applies). Rows are never deleted: pruning a tenant whose
    ledger is empty would race a concurrent first claim (the claim's DO NOTHING takes no lock on the existing
    row, so a delete in between would leave a live ledger row with no tenant row). The table is as large as the
    number of tenants that ever made a keyed request.

    No tenant_id RLS, deliberately, the posture of nexus.tuple_tenants (tuples-001-3) and service_tokens: the
    table names tenants and holds no tenant-owned data, and the arm that reads it must see every tenant's row.
    nexus_svc DML comes from the runAlways grants-nexus-svc.xml loop, with no edit there. nexus_diag gets no
    grant: nothing in it is diagnostic that service_tokens does not already show.

    Tenants that wrote ledger rows before this changeset are not in the table until they claim again. They keep
    the coverage they had: the retention arm still visits the reaper's tenants as well. Only such a tenant that
    also loses its last token before its next keyed request stays unretained, as every such tenant did before.
    There is no backfill: the ledger is FORCE RLS, so migration-time DML could not read it, and the table is
    DDL only, so this changeset needs no rehearsal seed.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-043-1" author="nexus-yye8l.21">
        <comment>Create request_ledger_tenants (RDR-222 ledger retention visits every ledger tenant)</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
CREATE TABLE nexus.request_ledger_tenants (
    tenant_id   TEXT        NOT NULL,
    first_seen  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    CONSTRAINT request_ledger_tenants_pk PRIMARY KEY (tenant_id)
);
        </sql>
        <rollback>DROP TABLE IF EXISTS nexus.request_ledger_tenants CASCADE</rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
